Z||000000||stimpy||01-23-2001||01:30 AM||||I'm looking around now for a headunit to replace my liberated Sony, and I really think I'll go with the Pioneer. What kind of prices have y'all paid? Do I need to order a mounting bracket? Does the Alarm+ feature work well? Thanks in advance for any feedback.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||01-23-2001||04:28 AM||||well, it's not a DEH-77dh, but I got a DEH-P5200 a few months ago.  Paid 250 for it at Best Buy.  Pretty much the same as the 77 except it's standard DIN size.  I love it, haven't had any problems.  While the DFS Alarm isn't the most sophisticated thing it does work pretty good, especially with the volume way up.  Until you forget you have it turned on, and get the bejeezus scared out of you when it goes off with you in the car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Everybody wants a normal life and a cool car.. <B>Most people settle for the car</B><P>I'm not dumb.  I just have a command of thoroughly useless information        <BR>AOL: LastMinuteBastrd<BR>AIM: Standard88||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||01-23-2001||04:42 AM||||I truly love my DEH77DH! You don't need a bracket for it although you probably have to drill a few extra holes, at least I needed to. The alarm works fairly well but as Standard says scares te sh!t out of you if you forget about it. It works by sounding loud tones over the speakers, but there's also a connection to connect to an alarm horn.<P>I paid $208 for it (best price I saw anywhere for it) <A HREF="http://www.marketplace4u.com/marketplace/product.asp?action=form&product=1024533" TARGET=_blank>here</A>. The price now is $222.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||01-23-2001||11:39 AM||||I have a new one (in box) that have offered sevaral times here for $200. Buyers come but at the end no money. I just went with a Kenwood system. If I don't sell it then I'll keep it for my near future V8 Fiero project (need to buy car first!). Or maybe sell it at Daytona...||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||01-23-2001||11:52 AM||||Not so hasty, mon ami.  Let me check on shipping costs. I think it's on like Donkey Kong. Does it come w/ documentation (manual, etc.)? Howzabout the wiring adapter? (would be pure bonus, the new ones don't have it.) <BR>Please God, let this happen. I need music!||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||01-23-2001||02:17 PM||||I love mine. A bit over-done on the features and getting to them.||||reg||14
